{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered","id":76332,"title":"Are Daemons overpowered","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-21T09:24:37-08:00","id":76332,"title":"Are Daemons overpowered","content":"I get that within the context of the demon game no, but in terms of a cross over game are they more overpowered than other archetypes such as vampire or mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2335-vulkan","name":"Vulkan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2335_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T11:02:14-08:00","id":76418,"title":"","content":"Probably not. Some of their core features are rather amazing, but are more passive responses, not the sort of thing you go in and bust around with. Embeds are the main powers most Demons will use all the time, and while some of them are quite powerful(I feel comfortable saying they are a little above Changeling's general power range as presented in the core), it's still not over-powered compared to the general spectrum.<br /> <br /> Exploits and certain Demonic Forms are anywhere from decently powerful to hella, with most of it not breaking anything, and the few that do are more specialized. The catch to how powerful some of these are lies in the fact that you're inviting trouble every time you use them.<br /> <br /> So maybe in some ways, but enough to raise an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T11:34:22-08:00","id":76451,"title":"","content":"well I'm in a cross over game and the other players believe my character is op on the basis I am a Daemon, I've tried explaining that the abilities are balanced by their negative but they accept it and then 5 minutes later start saying the same things, which is even more annoying as only me and one other member of the group has read the book and we both agree they aren't I just wanted to see who was with the majority","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2335-vulkan","name":"Vulkan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2335_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:30:13-08:00","id":76491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76418#post76418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not. Some of their core features are rather amazing, but are more passive responses, not the sort of thing you go in and bust around with. Embeds are the main powers most Demons will use all the time, and while some of them are quite powerful(I feel comfortable saying they are a little above Changeling's general power range as presented in the core), it's still not over-powered compared to the general spectrum.<br /> <br /> Exploits and certain Demonic Forms are anywhere from decently powerful to hella, with most of it not breaking anything, and the few that do are more specialized. The catch to how powerful some of these are lies in the fact that you're inviting trouble every time you use them.<br /> <br /> So maybe in some ways, but enough to raise an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be inclined to agree with you, but there are four powers that make me have to say that demons can (can be being the operating phrase here, let the records show lol) be the most overpowered force in the entire game. all you need are three embeds and one Demon form ability: Momentum, Just Bruised, Merciless Gunman, and Rivet Arm. Merciless Gunman and Rivet Arm in particular... my god that is friggen scary when you are facing most npc combatants. Granted that is just an example I've witnessed, so take it how you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:33:39-08:00","id":76494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulkan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76451#post76451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well I'm in a cross over game and the other players believe my character is op on the basis I am a Daemon, I've tried explaining that the abilities are balanced by their negative but they accept it and then 5 minutes later start saying the same things, which is even more annoying as only me and one other member of the group has read the book and we both agree they aren't I just wanted to see who was with the majority</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if your a Daemon, of course you're overpowered cause you're in the wrong universe! wh 40k is across the internet over yonder XD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T13:31:22-08:00","id":76526,"title":"","content":"I'll agree merciless gunman is op but we have already rebalanced that ourselves to be just 8 again, but even so killing npc in the bucket loads isnt really that much of an issue imo and it's only for down and dirty combat anyway, so anything that is an actual threat is still a threat, I see what you mean by rivet arm that could be abused so I can see what you mean if you were playing to power game you could do some horrible things with demon(fine I'll use the american spelling, damn yanks, *shakes fist) but when playing demon as it was intended all these horrible things(though few in number) wouldn't be used and most of the powers they use they don't have direct control of, lucky break for instance yeah you get something good but how is entirely up to the gm and abusing this as it states in the rules is bad for you.<br /> <br /> As for just bruised I'm not sure I agree I could understand it would be a big f you to some things but equally you heal damage like a human and take damage like a human, most other supernatural creatures start with a healing ability(at least from the books I have read) whereas demons do not, they do have that one embed but it's still not as powerful as vampire healing especially if they are ordo dracul. I would agree with it not being balanced probably, it should a percentage reduction rather than reducing it to 1 or 0, and the heal embed is ok but for healing aggravated damage unless your very powerful character it will take you a while.<br /> <br /> I agree with momentum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2335-vulkan","name":"Vulkan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2335_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T13:35:58-08:00","id":76528,"title":"","content":"Well the right daemon only has to stop doing it's job and wont start again the global economy could be in trouble, so yes.<br /> <br /> (I'm being completely serious, but also joking)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T13:36:31-08:00","id":76529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76494#post76494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well if your a Daemon, of course you're overpowered cause you're in the wrong universe! wh 40k is across the internet over yonder XD.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there are most definitely daemons in the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T14:05:47-08:00","id":76558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76529#post76529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, there are most definitely daemons in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm completely aware, I'm just yanking his chain. And this proves that a joke explained is no joke at all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T14:09:03-08:00","id":76563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76528#post76528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the right daemon only has to stop doing it's job and wont start again the global economy could be in trouble, so yes.<br /> <br /> (I'm being completely serious, but also joking)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the main timeline makes this mute, as Y2K is still doing his job lol. Though if all versions of him did so, we would have no problem with the timeline splits in Seattle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:16:49-08:00","id":76626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76491#post76491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be inclined to agree with you, but there are four powers that make me have to say that demons can (can be being the operating phrase here, let the records show lol) be the most overpowered force in the entire game. all you need are three embeds and one Demon form ability: Momentum, Just Bruised, Merciless Gunman, and Rivet Arm. Merciless Gunman and Rivet Arm in particular... my god that is friggen scary when you are facing most npc combatants. Granted that is just an example I've witnessed, so take it how you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very specialized demon. A player willing to specialize that much kind of deserves a certain amount of OP.<br /> <br /> Also, Merciless Gunman isn't that OP considering the context you get to use it in. It opens doors for when you could use the Down and Dirty ruleset, but asides from that it's not a godsend-at least not one we've seen before.<br /> <br /> Momentum works fairly well if you have a line up going on, but on it's own-well, how many successes do you get regularly on a roll? Two, three? THose turn into dice, so you're on average going to get about an extra success out of it. It helps, but you are looking at diminishing returns-unless, again, you have a whole crew of you just keep spamming the thing, in which case, good for you. A single chain break will screw you up though.<br /> <br /> Just Bruised and Rivet Gun, I got nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T17:01:01-08:00","id":76707,"title":"","content":"Demons are ridiculously powerful in very short bursts.<br /> <br /> Outside of &quot;just bruised&quot; there's not a lot that gives them a huge amount of staying power. Covers are pretty resilient to other supernatural powers (and is usually guaranteed to be higher than your Primum), but aren't generally any more physically resistant to being hit than a mortal outside of specific embeds/exploits. Some of the Demon form abilities give you lots of defence/armour/whatever, but manifesting those costs you a cover roll each time. A fully transformed Demon is terrifying (and deservedly so!), but at the cost of attracting God Machine Attention.<br /> <br /> Really, Demons are much more powerful when dealing with interpersonal relationships, getting places they don't belong and dealing with technology (which makes sense when dealing with a sub-genre based around spycraft)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T17:53:49-08:00","id":76741,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem with some of the demon things is that the writers neglected to include some resistances and such. If you start adding in resistance rolls, or call for Clash of Wills with things like Just Bruised, the effects become much less pronounced. Take a look at LOOK's houserules for demon - they're entirely dominated by adding in resistance rolls or subtracting from rolls.<br /> <br /> Demons with a gun man combat build are pretty good. That said... its about the only build they have magic powers to back up! Sure, you can get +2 Strength, armor, and a blade arm from demon form... but those are pretty much replaceable by just buying armor and a blade, and a vampire's blood buff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T18:34:07-08:00","id":76761,"title":"","content":"I would say Demons in general, in terms of active abilities, are slightly more powerful than Changelings, somewhat less powerful than Geist. (Although yeah... both splats are pre-GMC so it doesn't say all that much...) And Demons don't scale all that well with experience. Nonetheless, their superb resistance while in cover and they are thematically, and in their many abilities, superb liars and that's their strength. (and I think demonic embeds lacking the contested resistance is part of that theme.)<br /> <br /> All in all, I would not call Demons overpowered. No. That's the word for Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T18:41:13-08:00","id":76763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76761#post76761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All in all, I would not call Demons overpowered. <b>No. That's the word for Mage.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Please let's not do this shitty annoying thing.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T18:50:37-08:00","id":76768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76763#post76763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Please let's not do this shitty annoying thing.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whoops sorry<br /> <br /> What I meant is, Mages are, by the rules, the splat with most power and versatility.<br /> <br /> I used the term 'overpowered' in the context the original poster used, and if 'overpowered' could potentially be used to describe the demons, I guessed that for the mages as well. But if you disagree that mages are not any more powerful than demons or anyone else, you could have told that without being extra angry about that.<br /> <br /> Still. I'm sorry if that offended you or anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T18:57:35-08:00","id":76774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76768#post76768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used the term 'overpowered' in the context the original poster used, and if 'overpowered' could potentially be used to describe the demons, I guessed that for the mages as well. But if you disagree that mages are not any more powerful than demons or anyone else, you could have told that without being extra angry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mages are overpowered,&quot; in addition to being off-topic, has been an old and volatile argument since long before I joined the fandom a paltry five years ago. It's a topic-incendiary and a thread-derailer. <b>Don't.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T19:02:50-08:00","id":76782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76774#post76774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Mages are overpowered,&quot; in addition to being off-topic, has been an old and volatile argument since long before I joined the fandom a paltry five years ago. It's a topic-incendiary and a thread-derailer. <b>Don't.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>While I meant nothing like that, I do apologise and take that statement back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T19:08:56-08:00","id":76788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76741#post76741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem with some of the demon things is that the writers neglected to include some resistances and such. If you start adding in resistance rolls, or call for Clash of Wills with things like Just Bruised, the effects become much less pronounced. Take a look at LOOK's houserules for demon - they're entirely dominated by adding in resistance rolls or subtracting from rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Neglected&quot; isn't the word here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon The Descent, Pg 124</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resisting Embeds<br /> Most Embeds list a trait to subtract from the players roll, while a few are contested actions (Embeds that do not target a specific person do not apply resistance traits, obviously). <b>These resistance traits are optional</b>, however. Whether or not to use them is a Storyteller\u2019s decision, and that decision should be based on how challenging the action is, what the circumstances are, and who the target is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rules As Intended states that resisting a demon's power is not guaranteed, or necessarily intended to be resisted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T19:56:56-08:00","id":76815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76626#post76626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very specialized demon. A player willing to specialize that much kind of deserves a certain amount of OP.<br /> <br /> Also, Merciless Gunman isn't that OP considering the context you get to use it in. It opens doors for when you could use the Down and Dirty ruleset, but asides from that it's not a godsend-at least not one we've seen before.<br /> <br /> Momentum works fairly well if you have a line up going on, but on it's own-well, how many successes do you get regularly on a roll? Two, three? THose turn into dice, so you're on average going to get about an extra success out of it. It helps, but you are looking at diminishing returns-unless, again, you have a whole crew of you just keep spamming the thing, in which case, good for you. A single chain break will screw you up though.<br /> <br /> Just Bruised and Rivet Gun, I got nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to see what is specialized as I was not describing a single demon. Now if I was describing a particular demon's power set, then yes, but for here? I am unsure where you got the specialized from.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Down and Dirty rules aren't really hard to bring into play, so it's a lot more of a god send than you would realize, all things considered lol.<br /> <br /> Now as for Momentum, considering how I have party members who roll up to the double digits consistently ( through what I can only explain as black magic), Momentum is the destroyer of worlds in our game group. But as you said, it is a matter of context.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 02-21-2014, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T20:08:52-08:00","id":76820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76774#post76774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Mages are overpowered,&quot; in addition to being off-topic, has been an old and volatile argument since long before I joined the fandom a paltry five years ago. It's a topic-incendiary and a thread-derailer. <b>Don't.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean to point things out, but aren't you acting as a derailer as well by pointing this out? That's equally disruptive when you think about it. So is this comment as well. Huh, we're all in the wrong it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T20:39:54-08:00","id":76832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76815#post76815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fail to see what is specialized as I was not describing a single demon. Now if I was describing a particular demon's power set, then yes, but for here? I am unsure where you got the specialized from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specialized does not necessarily mean a specific demon or singular demon.<br /> <br /> A group of people can be specialized in a certain thing. For example, people -&gt; health care practitioners -&gt; doctors -&gt; surgeons -&gt; Cardiologists. and so on. Cardiologists are heart specialists and there can be many cardiologists.<br /> I'm also not, suggesting that the demon taking the powers/abilities in question is equal in degree of specialization as a cardiologist. The example was offered up merely to illustrate that many people can be considered &quot;specialized&quot;.<br /> <br /> ON TOPIC<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not a fan of X IS BETTER THAN Y arguments so .. let's see.. what else... hrmmm... ah.<br /> <br /> Forgive me if I've misread but I think the situation discussed earlier in the thread is not so much a balance issue but a group dynamics situation.<br /> <br /> I think that the group you're playing in might be running up against the tendency to fear the unknown/new things. It seems that the rest of the group can not/will not read the demon book and come to an opinion based on an independent examination of the material.<br /> Might I suggest that It's not so much that they think Demon is OP but that they haven't taken the opportunity to sit down and consider it.<br /> <br /> Of course, the preceeding is entirely my opinion without being involved. Which I don't really like to give out given those circumstances - but I just feel that the topic describes a group dynamic issue not an inter-supplement balance issue and the group dynamics portion hasn't been addressed.<br /> <br /> I do sympathize with your situation, though. A long time ago I was in a similar situation (though I was, perhaps, on the other end of it accusing a different supplement of being OP =\\ ). With time and exposure I hope the others in your group will come to realize that demons are nifty, fun, and interesting but not necessarily OP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","user":"Rixx","date":".  hate it when you notice spelling/grammar AFTER posting. 02-21-2014, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T22:19:46-08:00","id":76874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76815#post76815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fail to see what is specialized as I was not describing a single demon. Now if I was describing a particular demon's power set, then yes, but for here? I am unsure where you got the specialized from.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Down and Dirty rules aren't really hard to bring into play, so it's a lot more of a god send than you would realize, all things considered lol.<br /> <br /> Now as for Momentum, considering how I have party members who roll up to the double digits consistently ( through what I can only explain as black magic), Momentum is the destroyer of worlds in our game group. But as you said, it is a matter of context.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)Rixx answered this adequately.<br /> <br /> 2)I can't think of many situations where I've thrown my players into a situation that would be conceivably dealt with by the Down and Dirty rules, let alone where Merciless Gunman would be an even bigger boon. I'm not saying it isn't useful or that it's absolutely uncommon-one of my Demon characters will certainly start with this-but I think that it's one of those things that becomes a matter of discretion on the Storyteller's part-the utility of it's first purpose lies entirely in their hands.<br /> <br /> 3)I've had game sessions where that happens, and yeah, Momentum would devour worlds in those.<br /> <br /> I have also had sessions where players were rolling 10 to 12 dice and coming up with bupkiss.<br /> <br /> Since the actual probability of it is all useless, I'm kind of left to conclude, based on the theoretical statistics, that Momentum, on average, is worth about an additional success on each use. Which is great in theory, but hardly game breaking.<br /> <br /> But yeah, context.<br /> <br /> I will say this: Demons are a lot like changelings in how they can stack the deck. Some of these things seem powerful but aren't all that much, but you start using them in connection to one another and start building up *cough* momentum, and a demon can really turn into a freight train.<br /> <br /> PS: Satchel is right, by the way-even an innocent mention of &quot;Mages are overpowered&quot; tends to stir passions to a frothing, wrathful mess.<br /> <br /> I find it interesting, as a side note, that the idea of Demons and Mages being the most commonly talked about OP characters is hilarious, seeing as both of them are the only ones who risk consequences each time they go hardball with their powers. The reward comes with risk other characters types just don't have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-22-2014, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T23:08:15-08:00","id":76883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76874#post76874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting, as a side note, that the idea of Demons and Mages being the most commonly talked about OP characters is hilarious, seeing as both of them are the only ones who risk consequences each time they go hardball with their powers. The reward comes with risk other characters types just don't have.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Demon's case, failing your consequences and losing cover/gaining conditions that are negative is quite...terrifying. Blown condition? Can't use your covers to spoof things at all. Betrayed? Give a former ally 8-again against you for *every* roll against you. Hunted? Send in the <b>Rank 5</b> freaking Angel to hunt you. Blackballed/Flagged/Surveilled are all bad, but not quite immediately catastrophic.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the conditions that can be caused while in Demon form. Demonic Rage? No Mental/Social Actions. At all. You can only attack. Or do other physical actions at -2. Aetheric Bleed? Let's drain out all of our magic juju. Even the disconnect can be nasty, penalising every social roll.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Demons can bring immense power to bear, but if they push the boundaries too much they get exceptionally dire consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T00:59:57-08:00","id":76909,"title":"","content":"Well thanks for all the replies, I'm glad it's not just me seeing demons and going I like your lore so you aren't overpowered.<br /> <br /> I did make the argument that yeah they have these powerful abilities but bad stuff happens if abuse them with compromise roles and conditions, but they simply decided they weren't penalties.<br /> <br /> It didn't really matter as the GM had already been convinced they weren't overpowered as I'd made sure he was aware of abusing powers or simply using them in some case and their negatives. I was only asking to make sure it wasn't just me being silly.<br /> <br /> But thanks again for all the replies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2335-vulkan","name":"Vulkan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2335_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T01:46:25-08:00","id":76924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76741#post76741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Take a look at LOOK's houserules for demon - they're entirely dominated by adding in resistance rolls or subtracting from rolls...</div> </div> </div> </div>For those looking, see my sig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T02:05:18-08:00","id":76930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulkan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76909#post76909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well thanks for all the replies, I'm glad it's not just me seeing demons and going I like your lore so you aren't overpowered.<br /> <br /> I did make the argument that yeah they have these powerful abilities but bad stuff happens if abuse them with compromise roles and conditions, but they simply decided they weren't penalties.<br /> <br /> It didn't really matter as the GM had already been convinced they weren't overpowered as I'd made sure he was aware of abusing powers or simply using them in some case and their negatives. I was only asking to make sure it wasn't just me being silly.<br /> <br /> But thanks again for all the replies</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For one I thought those penalties against the demon were horrendous. I guess it really is at the hand of the GM though. And, even if with high manipulation and wits, Cover ratings tend to plummet unless the players are being careful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76909#post76909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Neglected&quot; isn't the word here.<br /> The Rules As Intended states that resisting a demon's power is not guaranteed, or necessarily intended to be resisted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I am also for leaving them as written, and I am pretty sure they didn't &quot;neglect&quot; the resistences... and if the rolls are not contested, it's that for a reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","user":"torete","date":". 02-22-2014, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T05:53:34-08:00","id":77011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76874#post76874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)Rixx answered this adequately.<br /> <br /> 2)I can't think of many situations where I've thrown my players into a situation that would be conceivably dealt with by the Down and Dirty rules, let alone where Merciless Gunman would be an even bigger boon. I'm not saying it isn't useful or that it's absolutely uncommon-one of my Demon characters will certainly start with this-but I think that it's one of those things that becomes a matter of discretion on the Storyteller's part-the utility of it's first purpose lies entirely in their hands.<br /> <br /> 3)I've had game sessions where that happens, and yeah, Momentum would devour worlds in those.<br /> <br /> I have also had sessions where players were rolling 10 to 12 dice and coming up with bupkiss.<br /> <br /> Since the actual probability of it is all useless, I'm kind of left to conclude, based on the theoretical statistics, that Momentum, on average, is worth about an additional success on each use. Which is great in theory, but hardly game breaking.<br /> <br /> But yeah, context.<br /> <br /> I will say this: Demons are a lot like changelings in how they can stack the deck. Some of these things seem powerful but aren't all that much, but you start using them in connection to one another and start building up *cough* momentum, and a demon can really turn into a freight train.<br /> <br /> PS: Satchel is right, by the way-even an innocent mention of &quot;Mages are overpowered&quot; tends to stir passions to a frothing, wrathful mess.<br /> <br /> I find it interesting, as a side note, that the idea of Demons and Mages being the most commonly talked about OP characters is hilarious, seeing as both of them are the only ones who risk consequences each time they go hardball with their powers. The reward comes with risk other characters types just don't have.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Agreed.<br /> 2. You are absolutely correct, though also remember that with down and dirty rules it's equally initiated by the players as it is scripted by the ST, or at least with the people I've played with they sure seem to be capable of working interactions into favorable outcomes such as that hahaha.<br /> 3. It's hella scary and funny at the same time isn't it?<br /> <br /> Well... it depends on the number of dice the person has on average to roll. for example from what I've seen, if a person has five dice, it often comes to pass that the person rolling scores about two to three successes, more so if they roll well ( though again, with my group there is apparently a sorcerer due to the black magic they must surely be casting to get 5+ successes nearly every single roll..)). You are completely right that a person could roll that many dice and come up with nada.. though for some reason, the law of averages seems to be Ensorcelled by my players lol.<br /> <br /> Demons are like changelings, and that fact makes me seriously consider running a changeling/demon crossover at some point, mainly to tease one of my players who thinks that Changelings would always try to kill Demons on sight simply due to the fact that they can perform Soul Pacts ( This player is odd, he seems to forget about in character and out of character discretion when it comes to role playing, but that is either here nor there.)<br /> <br /> PS. I know, I've been around long enough to see it as well, but the thing is I do not take well to people addressing such posters in blatantly rude manners as Satchel routinely does. There is educating a person on how to avoid mistakes, then there is being hostile, which I don't agree with. I respect the man immensely, but I am not afraid to critique his etiquette on the forums, just as I am not afraid to be criticized on how I post either XD.<br /> <br /> And I share your sense of amusement, it is indeed funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 02-22-2014, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T06:10:13-08:00","id":77019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76788#post76788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Neglected&quot; isn't the word here.<br /> <br /> The Rules As Intended states that resisting a demon's power is not guaranteed, or necessarily intended to be resisted.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, I feel it is neglected is the right word. Why? Because if its optionally applied.... then they should have been listed as an option for every power. They did not do so.<br /> <br /> Lets say that we have a case of using Bystander Effect. One PC decides that, hey, he wants to kill a human in a bar by using the Embed. There is another PC nearby, who's witnessing the assassination. By the rules, that PC has NO option to resist the Bystander Effect. He's not related to person being killed. This is a concern. There should be some Condition or the like covering this event. It may be rare, but it should be covered in the event it does.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the Embeds follow in the same vein. Using Cause and Effect against an NPC without a resistance of some kind is fine, but a fellow PC? One person employing Cool Head Prevail when the rest of the party wants to go kill happy?<br /> <br /> The Embeds tend to assume that you're against certain kinds of opponents. And that these opponents generally should be cultist mooks or pawns. Ergo, the lack of resistances. Ergo, Merciless Gunman's main use in mook killing. When used against fellow PCs, or, hells, even major NPC demons/angels? No, that's not right; it is highly unthematic and makes little sense to me. Hells, the whole raison d'etre of Conditions was to cover these very situations! I'm going to stick by my choice of words and say that these situations were neglected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T06:21:16-08:00","id":77024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rixx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=76832#post76832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Specialized does not necessarily mean a specific demon or singular demon.<br /> <br /> A group of people can be specialized in a certain thing. For example, people -&gt; health care practitioners -&gt; doctors -&gt; surgeons -&gt; Cardiologists. and so on. Cardiologists are heart specialists and there can be many cardiologists.<br /> I'm also not, suggesting that the demon taking the powers/abilities in question is equal in degree of specialization as a cardiologist. The example was offered up merely to illustrate that many people can be considered &quot;specialized&quot;.<br /> <br /> ON TOPIC<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not a fan of X IS BETTER THAN Y arguments so .. let's see.. what else... hrmmm... ah.<br /> <br /> Forgive me if I've misread but I think the situation discussed earlier in the thread is not so much a balance issue but a group dynamics situation.<br /> <br /> I think that the group you're playing in might be running up against the tendency to fear the unknown/new things. It seems that the rest of the group can not/will not read the demon book and come to an opinion based on an independent examination of the material.<br /> Might I suggest that It's not so much that they think Demon is OP but that they haven't taken the opportunity to sit down and consider it.<br /> <br /> Of course, the preceeding is entirely my opinion without being involved. Which I don't really like to give out given those circumstances - but I just feel that the topic describes a group dynamic issue not an inter-supplement balance issue and the group dynamics portion hasn't been addressed.<br /> <br /> I do sympathize with your situation, though. A long time ago I was in a similar situation (though I was, perhaps, on the other end of it accusing a different supplement of being OP =\\ ). With time and exposure I hope the others in your group will come to realize that demons are nifty, fun, and interesting but not necessarily OP</div> </div> </div> </div>I thank you for your thoughts on the matter, they brought a lot of things to the fore I didn't consider right away, I greatly appreciate it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T07:33:19-08:00","id":77054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=77011#post77011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Agreed.<br /> 2. You are absolutely correct, though also remember that with down and dirty rules it's equally initiated by the players as it is scripted by the ST, or at least with the people I've played with they sure seem to be capable of working interactions into favorable outcomes such as that hahaha.<br /> 3. It's hella scary and funny at the same time isn't it?<br /> <br /> Well... it depends on the number of dice the person has on average to roll. for example from what I've seen, if a person has five dice, it often comes to pass that the person rolling scores about two to three successes, more so if they roll well ( though again, with my group there is apparently a sorcerer due to the black magic they must surely be casting to get 5+ successes nearly every single roll..)). You are completely right that a person could roll that many dice and come up with nada.. though for some reason, the law of averages seems to be Ensorcelled by my players lol.<br /> <br /> Demons are like changelings, and that fact makes me seriously consider running a changeling/demon crossover at some point, mainly to tease one of my players who thinks that Changelings would always try to kill Demons on sight simply due to the fact that they can perform Soul Pacts ( This player is odd, he seems to forget about in character and out of character discretion when it comes to role playing, but that is either here nor there.)<br /> <br /> PS. I know, I've been around long enough to see it as well, but the thing is I do not take well to people addressing such posters in blatantly rude manners as Satchel routinely does. There is educating a person on how to avoid mistakes, then there is being hostile, which I don't agree with. I respect the man immensely, but I am not afraid to critique his etiquette on the forums, just as I am not afraid to be criticized on how I post either XD.<br /> <br /> And I share your sense of amusement, it is indeed funny.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really agree wholeheartedly that Demons and Changelings are, in many ways, so alike that it begs crossover games between them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I am also planning to definitely running them. Then again, what I noticed is that Demons have little bit of every splat in them - Compromise as Paradox writ different, Demonic forms as an alternative of Werewolf forms, limited Pacts and cheap, smaller powers like the Changelings have, an (very limited) ability to have Primum at 10 (for a very short time, though) being very loosely like Mummies starting at Sekhem 10, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T07:46:38-08:00","id":77060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=77019#post77019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, I feel it is neglected is the right word. Why? Because if its optionally applied.... then they should have been listed as an option for every power. They did not do so.<br /> <br /> Lets say that we have a case of using Bystander Effect. One PC decides that, hey, he wants to kill a human in a bar by using the Embed. There is another PC nearby, who's witnessing the assassination. By the rules, that PC has NO option to resist the Bystander Effect. He's not related to person being killed. This is a concern. There should be some Condition or the like covering this event. It may be rare, but it should be covered in the event it does.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the Embeds follow in the same vein. Using Cause and Effect against an NPC without a resistance of some kind is fine, but a fellow PC? One person employing Cool Head Prevail when the rest of the party wants to go kill happy?<br /> <br /> The Embeds tend to assume that you're against certain kinds of opponents. And that these opponents generally should be cultist mooks or pawns. Ergo, the lack of resistances. Ergo, Merciless Gunman's main use in mook killing. When used against fellow PCs, or, hells, even major NPC demons/angels? No, that's not right; it is highly unthematic and makes little sense to me. Hells, the whole raison d'etre of Conditions was to cover these very situations! I'm going to stick by my choice of words and say that these situations were neglected.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing about Merciless Gunman though, it is explictly written that against PCs or Angels or any major enemies that won't utilize Down and Dirty Combat, the effect changes to just firearm attack with 8-again.<br /> <br /> See, I do think that since the resistance or subtraction have not been listed as an option for every power, especially because designers intended for some powers to be resisted/contested. If ALL of those powers did not have any resistance options, I would have said the same. But I think the distinction itself means that the designers did intend it, and I think it could be what gives demon an edge. Of course I might be wrong and the designers could have left them out by mistake, but I don't think that's the case as of now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T09:06:31-08:00","id":77106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=77019#post77019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, I feel it is neglected is the right word. Why? Because if its optionally applied.... then they should have been listed as an option for every power. They did not do so.<br /> <br /> Lets say that we have a case of using Bystander Effect. One PC decides that, hey, he wants to kill a human in a bar by using the Embed. There is another PC nearby, who's witnessing the assassination. By the rules, that PC has NO option to resist the Bystander Effect. He's not related to person being killed. This is a concern. There should be some Condition or the like covering this event. It may be rare, but it should be covered in the event it does.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the Embeds follow in the same vein. Using Cause and Effect against an NPC without a resistance of some kind is fine, but a fellow PC? One person employing Cool Head Prevail when the rest of the party wants to go kill happy?<br /> <br /> The Embeds tend to assume that you're against certain kinds of opponents. And that these opponents generally should be cultist mooks or pawns. Ergo, the lack of resistances. Ergo, Merciless Gunman's main use in mook killing. When used against fellow PCs, or, hells, even major NPC demons/angels? No, that's not right; it is highly unthematic and makes little sense to me. Hells, the whole raison d'etre of Conditions was to cover these very situations! I'm going to stick by my choice of words and say that these situations were neglected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Hat Matt, one of the big developers for this, has a philosophy in regards to this: If it'd be stupid to have it play out that way, then don't have it play out that way.<br /> <br /> Demon makes the assumption that the Storyteller is going to be involved and call for rolls as appropriate to the feel of the scenario. The rules are, after all, guidelines really, and if someone should be able to respond to a power they couldn't otherwise do, then you damn the rules and let them respond.<br /> <br /> Granted, this attitude may not be made plain in discussing Embeds, but it is a reasonable assumption, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T10:17:18-08:00","id":77171,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Granted, this attitude may not be made plain in discussing Embeds, but it is a reasonable assumption, actually. </div> </div> </div> Its one that I do make - that there should be. However, in the kind of situation we were discussing? Embeds really weren't designed with that situation in mind.<br /> <br /> And that's the issue when you're trying to compare the games. Demons work as spies, and are rather underhanded. They're not meant to have their Embeds be obvious. They're designed with that in mind. However, when they're used in ways beyond what was originally built into the design? Like a theoretical white room mash up? </span><br /> <br /> Well, its less theoretical when playing in a crossover game, where everyone can have a separate PC splat. And, if a demon and vampire PC did come to blows, I have to question how the Just Bruised would work in comparison to a Vampire with Vigor. Or Cool Head Prevail versus a frenzy trigger, and wanting to indulge said trigger, and similar.<br /> <br /> Its situations like these that players will come up with, and really don't fit into the usual mold the powers were intended for. And that's what causes things like, &quot;oh, avoiding resistance rolls in a fight is what gives demons an edge!&quot; No, its not so much an edge. That's not the intent - that's just a line for making the story flow faster and smoother. No everyday mortals getting lucky rolls and taking down a demon. That's not thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-22-2014, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T15:09:13-08:00","id":77348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=77106#post77106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Hat Matt, one of the big developers for this, has a philosophy in regards to this: If it'd be stupid to have it play out that way, then don't have it play out that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matt was co-developer for <b>Demon</b>, along with Rose Bailey.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T17:07:11-08:00","id":77408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=77019#post77019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Lets say that we have a case of using Bystander Effect. One PC decides that, hey, he wants to kill a human in a bar by using the Embed. There is another PC nearby, who's witnessing the assassination. By the rules, that PC has NO option to resist the Bystander Effect. He's not related to person being killed. This is a concern. There should be some Condition or the like covering this event. It may be rare, but it should be covered in the event it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then if it matters that PCs resist it, you either perform a Clash of Wills (for contradictory powers) or you can have the generic powerstat resistance for supernatural abilities come into play, which are generic WoD rules that applies to every game with characters that have a Powerstat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">And that's the issue when you're trying to compare the games. Demons work as spies, and are rather underhanded. They're not meant to have their Embeds be obvious. They're designed with that in mind. However, when they're used in ways beyond what was originally built into the design? Like a theoretical white room mash up? </span> </div> </div> </div>The Devs have stated on multiple occasions that they don't feel that the 'white room mashup' is actually important, helpful or useful. They've stated multiple times that they don't think inter-genre 'balance' is important at all, and that if something is bad for crossover but good for the individual game, they'll do the thing that is good for the individual game.<br /> <br /> If you're using something outside the design specs then the onus is on you (yes, you) to fit together the unfitting pieces to get a game that you (and your players) want to play. I mean, does it really matter that a Geist can tear the spleen from everyone from a Vampire to a Werewolf to a Changeling? I mean, this is something that comes up everytime someone asks 'I want to do a game with X and Y, but Y is more powerful than X, help?' There's no clean fit, easy solution or whatever. You're expected to houserule here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T17:16:01-08:00","id":77412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=77348#post77348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Matt was co-developer for <b>Demon</b>, along with Rose Bailey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence big.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T01:31:28-08:00","id":78166,"title":"","content":"Well if anyone is interested I had a game on saturday and I made more compromise rolls in each scene than the other players made humanity/integrity/whatever other morality system they have in the whole game.<br /> <br /> Not to mention combat is a pain even with just bruised taking damage isn't very good, especially if you don't have high medicine as you I couldn't heal as fast as the other pc or have anywhere near as much health as the werewolves, so unless you have bullet proof armour guns are gonna keep you down, not to mention you can be incapacitated if you fill with bashing and with lethal damage you are incapacitated and start filling up with aggravated, which is really bad when your allies are a werewolf and a skinchanger, neither of which can stop you bleeding out. And full transformation isn't a good idea unless you have to, and partial transformation is expensive you really can end up limping home while the other supernaturals are like &quot;silly human guns are bad for you&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2335-vulkan","name":"Vulkan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2335_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T02:08:34-08:00","id":78190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulkan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=78166#post78166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if anyone is interested I had a game on saturday and I made more compromise rolls in each scene than the other players made humanity/integrity/whatever other morality system they have in the whole game.<br /> <br /> Not to mention combat is a pain even with just bruised taking damage isn't very good, especially if you don't have high medicine as you I couldn't heal as fast as the other pc or have anywhere near as much health as the werewolves, so unless you have bullet proof armour guns are gonna keep you down, not to mention you can be incapacitated if you fill with bashing and with lethal damage you are incapacitated and start filling up with aggravated, which is really bad when your allies are a werewolf and a skinchanger, neither of which can stop you bleeding out. And full transformation isn't a good idea unless you have to, and partial transformation is expensive you really can end up limping home while the other supernaturals are like &quot;silly human guns are bad for you&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, Demon having more compromise roll than anyone is the theme of the game, and also the reason that Demons are the only ones who can have multiple cover. And you are right, demons are not all that great at fighting, unless you are super-specialized with firearms. I do think this too is part of the theme, as Demons are liars and dealers, and not as good fighters than just about anyone (except maybe for changelings, which I do think the potential for combat powers are about equal.) Also, Demonic Forms are not really all that great bonuses, and some really great Forms are those of utility, rather than combat.<br /> <br /> I do think Demons are quite potent, but I also think their strength does not come from combat power either. Their utilities, however, are stellar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","user":"torete","date":". 02-24-2014, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T04:14:33-08:00","id":78220,"title":"","content":"Yeah... demons don't do as well with direct fights. There's too large of a chance that you're calling for compromise rolls and drawing more angels to your scene; not something you want added on to whomever you're already fighting. <br /> <br /> Even a gunner build is best designed for hit and run tactics. Check Backdrop's best use is to give you time to keep someone from shooting you after your position is compromised by you shooting. In a direct, straight fight, you're just as hampered as the other guy from the aiming requirement; heaven forbid if your opponents use Suppresive Fire! So, you want to shoot, hide, shoot again. <br /> <br /> Heck, I think one of their most potent effects (Cool Heads Prevail) specifically prevents combat. Use that against an Angel after Going Loud? Could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-24-2014, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T07:58:20-08:00","id":78303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=77412#post77412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence big.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I was speaking for clarity only, not to correct you. Sorry if it came across that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T08:11:06-08:00","id":78314,"title":"","content":"Skimmed through most of the thread...not sure what the fuss is about. As a ST/GM (whatever you want to call it) I adhere to a simple rule of thumb when it comes to any supernatural powers used on other supernaturals (even subtle powers that don't normally allow resistance rolls) ... CLASH OF WILLS. One of the best mechanics in the game. Consistently keeps players from feeling railroaded. So in all of the examples of Demon A uses subtle power Z in the presence of Demon B ... Clash of Wills to notice. Also, always remember that just because a player notices a power has gone off doesn't imply that they have any info on the source. This principle extends to cross-overs (my favorite way to play). I also like to tinker with game mechanics in my spare time so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T11:38:51-08:00","id":78470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=77408#post77408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Devs have stated on multiple occasions that they don't feel that the 'white room mashup' is actually important, helpful or useful. They've stated multiple times that they don't think inter-genre 'balance' is important at all, and that if something is bad for crossover but good for the individual game, they'll do the thing that is good for the individual game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a weird relationship with crossover. I actually really like it, and I like it when the rules mesh. That's why Clash of Wills is useful - it's nice to have a standardized way for powers to relate to one another that an ST can use as a default. So crossover and a certain degree of &quot;balance&quot; is good. <br /> <br /> But &quot;balance&quot; isn't white-room balance. White-room balance (that is, &quot;devoid of any context, are these character types equally capable, usually at murdering one another&quot;) is stupid. It's stupid because a) it never comes up in play, EVER, and b) players are clever, and they spot things like the Endless Blood Point Loop that shows up in the Coils of Blood in VtR. <br /> <br /> We're not going to spot all those things. Ever. No matter how good we are or who we have proof, there are *always* going to be things that look &quot;overpowered&quot; because a player reads them and thinks, &quot;oh, shit, I know how to exploit that.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, instead, I ask - I insist - that players consider where their exploit is awesome and thematic, or just a way to go &quot;BROKE YOUR GAME LOL&quot; at the Storyteller. If the form, awesome. If the latter, I don't care. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T13:17:23-08:00","id":78532,"title":"","content":"I admit, whenever I think of Demon and &quot;BROKE YOUR GAME LOL&quot; gameplay, I immediately think of Going Loud+Rain of Blood. A tacnuke in every Demon's pocket. ^_^<br /> <br /> As to if Demons are overpowered, man that's a whole other kettle of fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T17:09:46-08:00","id":79769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=78303#post78303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. I was speaking for clarity only, not to correct you. Sorry if it came across that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. You're good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T17:12:21-08:00","id":79772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=78303#post78303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. I was speaking for clarity only, not to correct you. Sorry if it came across that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all, you're good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T00:56:25-07:00","id":94776,"title":"","content":"I think the most overpowered embed is Shift Consequence. Considering it can be used to basically shift any state to anyone else, that seems pretty brutal. Not to mention with the inspired condition, if you're good with a gun those exceptional successes are gonna come up a LOT and that 8- again rule on your fire arms just became 8- again + rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2553-kai","name":"Kai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2553_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T03:16:22-07:00","id":94828,"title":"","content":"Since several games haven't had the GodMachine rule update yet, it's hard to have a real basis of comparison. My first answer though is no, not really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T05:45:36-07:00","id":94875,"title":"","content":"My biggest issue in the crossover isn't that Demons have kewl powers.<br /> <br /> It's that the penalties for using them is drawing down the God-Machine. What other splats are particularly capable of dealing with a high rank angel or multiple lower ranked ones?<br /> <br /> The Demon messes up and the entire party has to deal with it. Or abandon the PC.<br /> <br /> Glitches are more personal, they're a 'punishment' to the individual, calling in a bad guy hit squad is impersonal, it affects everyone. Sure it's a drawback, but it;s not one you will be dealing with alone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T17:37:45-07:00","id":95302,"title":"","content":"Its not that different than the whole &quot;Only a mage can counter a mage&quot; thing. With paradox so weak, most of what restricts mages from stomping all over the place is their society, attracting Seers, and the like. Mages tend to be paranoid about their real names... with other mages - its not like a vampire learning an Awakened's name can do anything magical with it.<br /> <br /> Thus, the work around in a crossover game is to either 1) buff up and tweak the &quot;true name&quot; and paradox weaknesses, 2) include the overseers watching you, or 3) new weakness.<br /> <br /> If you're running a crossover game with other splats, then I suggest tweaking the reason why losing cover is bad. For instance... well, in Inferno, those particular brand of demons cannot exist in reality for extended periods of time without reality forcing them back to their native plane. They need some kind of mallus loci to protect them. Expanding on this idea... a demon without Cover cannot exist in reality, and will be ejected. If you hit zero Cover, or go loud, you have one scene to adopt a new cover of some kind. A backup Cover, or forge a new one, something. If you don't, you are &quot;banished&quot; from reality.<br /> <br /> Individual failures won't bring down hunter angels, but instead absolutely manifest glitches, or they temporarily lose access to any social merits or relations that don't know about the demon's true nature.<br /> <br /> Also, I suggest making holy water / objects deal agg / unravel Cover against Unchained, with the rational that &quot;true blessed&quot; items were made by the God Machine and his angels to hunt Unchained. Which could work.<br /> <br /> EDIT - A bit harsh, perhaps, but Demon is also the only game where its possible to play a 0 cover character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-20-2014, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T18:08:06-07:00","id":95310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/76332-are-daemons-overpowered?p=94875#post94875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What other splats are particularly capable of dealing with a high rank angel or multiple lower ranked ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same ones who are capable of dealing with ten to fifteen cultists, which you may recall has been an option for Hunted for some time.<br /> <br /> Also, a pointed reminder that the Lost can <i>summon the hunting party of one or more Old Gods</i> with a comparatively inexpensive non-chained four-dot power <i>because that is its own drawback</i>, and this is near-duplicated by a power held by an antagonist-type which can perfectly pass for human and may or may not be in contact with a particular Stranger.<br /> <br /> Further, <i>of course crossover has complications.</i> The nWoD's existed for nearly a decade with the understanding that crossover is not the default mode of play that the books are written to facilitate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-20-2014, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T04:55:13-07:00","id":95521,"title":"","content":"I personally feel that the problem, in this case of crossover-ness, has more to do with having to bring in outside forces to hunt the PC party because of a slip up, and not because of anything else, cultist or not. Going back to the mage comparison, having to bring outside mage forces to deal with a mage going vulgar doesn't really help out a good number of crossover stories, and, in fact, often hinders them. <br /> <br /> So, it doesn't matter so much that you're getting attacked by cultists. It matters that their weakness is inherently tied to their setting, and is required for any game that may not want such a thing at any point.<br /> <br /> Granted, I don't know how well playing a Demon in a crossover game is going to work out in the long run anyways. Much like Werewolves are irrevocably tied to Loci and the Hisil for their essence and Sin-Eaters to resolving ghostly anchors and actively serving as a psychopomp, Demons -must- hunt angels and hunt down Infrastructure for aether. Vampires can grab anything alive, pretty much; mages have a million ways to regain mana; prometheans just need a battery or wall socket; changelings can eat emotions; Hunters recover willpower as normal. Demons, Sin-Eaters, and Werewolves, however, are irrevocably tied to their spiritual-antagonists. They cannot thrive outside of dealing with them. Given that the Unchained's powers are not only reliant on dealing with God's cults and angels, but also their weakness and a good chunk of the Agendas? I'm not sure how it would play out in the long run.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not really sure what my point is anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T06:38:42-07:00","id":96316,"title":"","content":"Question: &quot;Are Demons Overpowered&quot;<br /> <br /> Context: Within Demon.<br /> Answer: Yes, but the God-Machine is even more Overpowered.<br /> <br /> Context: Crossing the streams, Demons are the antagonist:<br /> Answer: Antagonists are always gauged compared to the PCs, regardless of strict amount of XP used to build them.<br /> <br /> Context: Crossing the streams, Demons are a protagonist:<br /> Answer: As Scutarii said: &quot;It's that the penalties for using them is drawing down the God-Machine. What other splats are particularly capable of dealing with a high rank angel or multiple lower ranked ones? The Demon messes up and the entire party has to deal with it. Or abandon the PC.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}